(A handle opened at a number borrows that descriptor, and Close closes the
descriptor itself. The compiler warns at each Close below; the program still
compiles and runs exactly as written.)

Open a file for reading called keyboard at 0.
Close keyboard.
Print "standard output is still open".

Open a file for writing called screen at 1.
Write "written before the close\n" to screen.
Close screen.
Print "not shown: standard output is closed now".
